/* book Worked example 2: Q: A water-sealed bell spirometer has a bell of inside cross-section 400 cm². During a slow vital capacity manoeuvre the bell rises 9.25 cm. The room is at 24 °C and 760 mmHg (water vapour pressure 22.4 mmHg). Find the vital capacity at ATPS and at BTPS.
   1. Volume at ATPS: V = A × Δh = 400 cm² × 9.25 cm = 3700 cm³ = 3.70 L.
   2. Pressure term: (760 − 22.4) / (760 − 47) = 737.6 / 713 = 1.0345.
   3. Temperature term: 310 / (273 + 24) = 310 / 297 = 1.0438.
   4. BTPS factor = 1.0345 × 1.0438 = 1.080; VBTPS = 3.70 × 1.080 = 4.00 L.
   Answer: VC = 3.70 L at ATPS and 4.00 L at BTPS; reporting the ATPS value would understate the lung by 8 %. */
